/*
# Window

A window inside a program: a raised surface with a title bar you drag it by and a button at
its end that closes it — and, when `resizable`, edges that resize it. It is the theme's
surface, hairline, rounding and shadow, as a dialog or a popover is, with the title bar the
same surface and a hairline under it.

It is also a world of its own. A menu, popover, dialog or sheet declared inside it opens
over it: above its content and past its edges, turning and scaling with it. A toast belongs
to the whole program and shows at the bottom of the App. Tab stays among the window's
controls; F6 moves to the next window, Shift-F6 back; a press inside it gives it the
keyboard, back on the control that last had focus there, and brings it to the front. A
dialog or sheet open in it holds back presses aimed at this window only — another window,
or what lies behind, still takes them. Esc closes it when focus is inside it and nothing
open inside it takes Esc first.

Its children go into its body, the pane below the title bar, and place themselves there as
in any view — give one a layout or a `padding` of its own. Whether it is open is state, by
the value pattern: `open` on its own, or `open = { … }` with `input` writing where your
state lives. Its `x`, `y`, `width` and `height` are its own to move and resize, so set them
as literals.

```declare
App [ width = 640, height = 360, fill = { provided("theme").background },
    notesOpen: boolean = true,
    Button [ x = 20, y = 316, label = "Show notes", disabled = { app.notesOpen },
        onClick() { app.notesOpen = true } ],
    Window [ x = 30, y = 30, width = 280, height = 190, title = "Settings",
        more: Menu [ items = { [ ({ id: "reset", label: "Reset" }), ({ id: "copy", label: "Copy settings" }) ] } ],
        View [ width = 100%, padding = 16,
            layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 12 ],
            Checkbox [ label = "Show line numbers" ],
            Checkbox [ label = "Wrap long lines" ],
            Button [ label = "More", menu = { parent.parent.more } ]
            ]
        ],
    Window [ x = 330, y = 60, width = 280, height = 220, title = "Notes", resizable = true,
        open = { app.notesOpen }, input(v: boolean) { app.notesOpen = v },
        View [ width = 100%, padding = 16,
            layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 10 ],
            TextInput [ width = 100%, placeholder = "Title" ]
            ]
        ]
    ]
```

### Without a frame

`frame = false` keeps the world and drops the frame: no surface, title bar, close button or
resize edges, and no bringing itself forward or closing on Esc — its fill, stroke, shadow
and rounding are yours, and so are moving, sizing and stacking it (`raise()` brings it to the
front). What a program with windows of its own design builds on — the Desktop app's are
these.

```declare
App [ width = 560, height = 260, fill = #E6E9EE,
    Window [ x = 40, y = 40, width = 240, height = 160, rotation = -4, frame = false, title = "Tilted",
        cornerRadius = 10, fill = white, shadow = { shadow(0, 6, 20, 0x00000033) },
        Text [ x = 16, y = 16, text = "A window of its own design" ],
        TextInput [ x = 16, y = 52, width = 200, accessibilityLabel = "Note" ]
        ]
    ]
```

## frame
Whether the window draws its frame — surface, title bar, close button, resize edges — and
behaves as a framed window does: brought forward when pressed or reached, closed by Esc.
`true` by default; `false` leaves the window bare for a frame of your own.

## title
The name in the title bar, and the window's name to a screen reader — give a frameless
window one too.

## closable
Whether it has a close button and closes on Esc.

## resizable
Whether its bottom and right edges and the corner between them resize it.

## minWidth
The narrowest a resize makes it.

## minHeight
The shortest a resize makes it.

## titleBarHeight
The height of the title bar; the body starts below it. None without a frame.

## open
Whether it is open. Constrain it to state of your own and override `input`, or leave it and
read it back.

## input()
**Where an opening or a closing goes**, receiving the new open state. The default writes
`open`; override it to own the destination.

## close()
Closes it, through `input(false)` — what the close button and Esc do.

## show()
Opens it, through `input(true)`, and brings it to the front.

## visible
Present while it is open.

## bringForward()
Brings it in front of the windows beside it — its siblings that are windows — and keeps it
beneath whatever its parent holds above them. A press in a framed window, focus arriving in
it and `show()` all call it.

## overlays
The layer the overlays declared inside the window open in — its `layer`, read by them as
`provided("overlays")`.

## enter()
Gives the window the keyboard: focus goes back to the control that last had it inside the
window, else to the first. What a press inside the window does; a program's own way of
bringing a window to the front calls it too.

## holdsFocus()
Whether focus is inside the window now, in a program it hosts included.

## focusScope
`region`: Tab stays among the window's controls, and F6 moves between windows.

## onPointerDown
A press inside the window, on nothing that takes it, gives the window the keyboard — and a
framed one comes to the front.

## defaultPlacement
`body`: its children go into the pane below the title bar (the whole window, without a
frame).

## width
360 to begin with; a resize changes it.

## height
240 to begin with; a resize changes it.

## accessibilityRole
`dialog`: a window that does not hold back the rest of the program.

## accessibilityLabel
The `title`, so a screen reader names the window.

## fill
The theme's `surface`; none without a frame.

## stroke
A hairline in the theme's `line`; none without a frame.

## cornerRadius
The theme's dialog rounding; none without a frame.

## shadow
The theme's dialog shadow; none without a frame.

## _dragX
**Internal.** Its `x` when a move began.

## _dragY
**Internal.** Its `y` when a move began.

## _sizeW
**Internal.** Its `width` when a resize began.

## _sizeH
**Internal.** Its `height` when a resize began.

## _moveStart()
**Internal.** The title bar's press: brings it to the front and notes where it started.

## _moveBy()
**Internal.** Moves it by the pointer's travel since the press, keeping its title bar within
its parent.

## _moveEnd()
**Internal.** The release: an interrupted move puts it back where it started.

## _sizeStart()
**Internal.** A resize edge's press.

## _sizeBy()
**Internal.** Resizes it by the pointer's travel since the press, along the edges the grabbed
one moves (`"r"`, `"b"` or `"rb"`), no smaller than the minimum.

## _sizeEnd()
**Internal.** The release: an interrupted resize puts the size back.
*/

/*
# WindowClose

The close button of a `Window`: a quiet round button with a small cross, filled only while
hovered or pressed.

```declare
App [ width = 300, height = 140, fill = { provided("theme").background },
    Window [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 260, height = 100, title = "Press the cross" ]
    ]
```

## width
A 24-pixel round target.

## height
A 24-pixel round target.

## cornerRadius
Round.

## fill
None at rest; the theme's `controlHovered` while hovered and `controlPressed` while pressed.

## accessibilityRole
`button`.

## accessibilityLabel
"Close".
*/

include [ "control.declare" ]

class Window [ width = 360, height = 240,
    accessibilityRole = dialog,
    accessibilityLabel = { title },
    focusScope = region,
    defaultPlacement = body,
    visible = { open },

    frame: boolean = true,
    title: string = "",
    closable: boolean = true,
    resizable: boolean = false,
    minWidth: number = 200,
    minHeight: number = 120,
    titleBarHeight: number = { frame ? 36 : 0 },

    fill = { frame ? provided("theme").surface : null },
    stroke = { frame ? stroke(1, provided("theme").line) : null },
    cornerRadius = { frame ? (provided("theme").dialogCornerRadius ?? provided("theme").menuCornerRadius + 2) : 0 },
    shadow = { frame ? (provided("theme").dialogShadow ?? provided("theme").menuShadow) : null },

    open: boolean = true,
    input(v: boolean) { open = v },
    close() { this.input(false) },
    show() { this.input(true); this.bringForward() },

    overlays: View? = { this.layer },

    holdsFocus() -> boolean { return Focus.holds(this) },

    enter() { if (!this.holdsFocus()) Focus.focusIn(this) },

    onPointerDown() {
        if (frame) this.bringForward()
        this.enter()
        },

    // in front of the windows beside it, and still beneath whatever the parent
    // keeps above its windows (the focus ring, the overlay layers)

    bringForward() {
        const kids = (this.parent as View).children
        let last = -1
        for (let i = 0; i < kids.length; i++) if (typeof (kids[i] as any).holdsFocus == "function") last = i
        if (last < 0 || kids[last] == this) return
        if (last + 1 < kids.length) this.raise(kids[last + 1] as View)
        else this.raise()
        },

    // moving and resizing: where the gesture began; the pointer's travel since
    // the press is the event's root-space delta

    _dragX: number = 0,
    _dragY: number = 0,
    _sizeW: number = 0,
    _sizeH: number = 0,

    _moveStart() {
        this.bringForward()
        this.enter()
        _dragX = x
        _dragY = y
        },
    _moveBy(dx: number, dy: number) {
        const p = this.parent as View
        x = Math.max(60 - width, Math.min(p.width - 60, _dragX + dx))
        y = Math.max(0, Math.min(p.height - titleBarHeight, _dragY + dy))
        },
    _moveEnd(canceled: boolean) { if (canceled) { x = _dragX; y = _dragY } },

    _sizeStart() {
        this.bringForward()
        this.enter()
        _sizeW = width
        _sizeH = height
        },
    _sizeBy(edges: string, dx: number, dy: number) {
        if (edges.indexOf("r") >= 0) width = Math.max(minWidth, _sizeW + dx)
        if (edges.indexOf("b") >= 0) height = Math.max(minHeight, _sizeH + dy)
        },
    _sizeEnd(canceled: boolean) { if (canceled) { width = _sizeW; height = _sizeH } },

    // the window's own pane: the body, which clips to the window's rounding
    // (its children's ignoreClip escapes it, as a band past the edge must), then
    // the title bar (so Tab reaches the content first and the close button
    // last), then the resize edges

    content: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%,

        body: View [ y = { classroot.titleBarHeight }, width = 100%, height = { parent.height - classroot.titleBarHeight },
            clip = true,
            cornerRadius = { classroot.frame ? [0, 0, classroot.cornerRadius as number, classroot.cornerRadius as number] : classroot.cornerRadius } ],

        titleBar: View [ width = 100%, height = { classroot.titleBarHeight }, visible = { classroot.frame },
            onPointerDown(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._moveStart() },
            onPointerMove(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._moveBy(e.deltaX, e.deltaY) },
            onPointerUp(e: PointerUpEvent) { classroot._moveEnd(e.canceled) },

            // leading, or centred where the theme centres a dialog's title

            caption: TextLabel [ wrap = false, clip = true, fontSize = 13, fontWeight = semibold,
                x = { provided("theme").dialogTextAlign == "center" ? 40 : 14 },
                width = { parent.width - this.x - 40 },
                textAlign = { provided("theme").dialogTextAlign == "center" ? "center" : "left" },
                textColor = { provided("theme").text },
                text = { classroot.title } ],

            closer: WindowClose [ x = { parent.width - this.width - 7 }, y = center,
                visible = { classroot.closable },
                press() { classroot.close() }
                ],

            rule: View [ y = { parent.height - 1 }, width = 100%, height = 1, fill = { provided("theme").line } ]
            ],

        // the resize edges: a band astride the frame line, and the corner, which
        // wins over both

        sizeRight: View [ visible = { classroot.frame && classroot.resizable }, ignoreClip = true, cursor = "ew-resize",
            x = { parent.width - 4 }, y = { classroot.titleBarHeight }, width = 8, height = { parent.height - classroot.titleBarHeight - 12 },
            onPointerDown(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeStart() },
            onPointerMove(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeBy("r", e.deltaX, e.deltaY) },
            onPointerUp(e: PointerUpEvent) { classroot._sizeEnd(e.canceled) }
            ],
        sizeBottom: View [ visible = { classroot.frame && classroot.resizable }, ignoreClip = true, cursor = "ns-resize",
            x = 0, y = { parent.height - 4 }, width = { parent.width - 12 }, height = 8,
            onPointerDown(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeStart() },
            onPointerMove(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeBy("b", e.deltaX, e.deltaY) },
            onPointerUp(e: PointerUpEvent) { classroot._sizeEnd(e.canceled) }
            ],
        sizeGrip: View [ visible = { classroot.frame && classroot.resizable }, ignoreClip = true, cursor = "nwse-resize",
            x = { parent.width - 16 }, y = { parent.height - 16 }, width = 20, height = 20,
            onPointerDown(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeStart() },
            onPointerMove(e: PointerEvent) { classroot._sizeBy("rb", e.deltaX, e.deltaY) },
            onPointerUp(e: PointerUpEvent) { classroot._sizeEnd(e.canceled) },
            draw(d: Draw) {
                d.strokeStyle = provided("theme").textFaint
                d.lineWidth = 1
                d.lineCap = "round"
                d.beginPath()
                d.moveTo(5, 13); d.lineTo(13, 5)
                d.moveTo(9, 13); d.lineTo(13, 9)
                d.stroke()
                }
            ]
        ],

    // above the content and outside its clip: what opens inside the window
    // paints here, past its edges

    layer: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, pointerEvents = "none" ],

    // Esc reaches this only when no overlay holds the keyboard: one open
    // inside the window takes it first

    escKeys: Keys [
        onKeyDown(e: KeyEvent) {
            if (e.key == "Escape" && classroot.frame && classroot.closable && classroot.open && classroot.holdsFocus()) classroot.close()
            }
        ],

    // focus arriving by F6 or a press on a control brings a framed window forward

    focusWatch: Focus [
        onFocusChange(v: View) { if (v != null && classroot.frame && classroot.holdsFocus()) classroot.bringForward() }
        ]
    ]


class WindowClose extends Control [ width = 24, height = 24, cornerRadius = 12,
    accessibilityRole = button,
    accessibilityLabel = "Close",
    fill = { pressed ? provided("theme").controlPressed : hovered ? provided("theme").controlHovered : null },
    CloseIcon [ x = center, y = center, iconSize = 14, ink = { provided("theme").textMuted } ]
    ]
